    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Bak'd by_ par Mona Cookies Inc.",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105817047992386559581/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUyxPnts8ac1AxWcBc6KhM9qgI39XjuSe8tLbNFbnr-4tY9DXT5=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "we love doing day trips from Montreal and this past Sunday was to various parts of this area ending at Vignoble d'Ovila.  We have gone to several wineries within 1-2 hours outside of Montreal, and have to say this was our best experience.  We were starting to give up on Quebec wines, but this place had great wines.  Spiros, gave us a very detailed tour of the whole process, explaining the grapes, leaves, the harvesting, the barreling, the elements that make a great wine and the perils of being in this business, the how and why.  It was very detailed and informative.  Open to any and all questions.  We took the wine tasting and outdoor oven pizza combo.  We sat outside (there is a beautiful inside section too and a tented section as well, where they host weddings and business meetings, or events). We had several whites and several red wines, each with a distinct flavour.  We opted for the D'ovila pizza and it was amazing. Perfect crust, cheese and sauce. As the sun was just starting to set I really felt like we were in Italy for a few hours.  Highly recommend this place.",
        "time": 1720546102,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Charlie Butler",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117685345876119983649/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV7dcUHEtAC72GkrpprsiqBLN2d-PDuK3J_dxEq0P-WUoUdNZsD=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "2 years ago",
        "text": "Extremely charming vinyard. We stopped in for pizza and degustation. Food is served in the quaint setting. The pizza was freshly made in front of us and was absolutely fantastic (I’m still thinking about it now!) The owners were incredibly attentive, friendly and spent time explaining their different wines and the history of their vinyard. Can’t wait to visit again. And there’s a sweet dog there too. What’s not to love?",
        "time": 1690083865,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Yurii Chernyshov",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117747068070462032612/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXpe7Fs1CFV_5o5DyatzcU9xLma2yf-g8VlKZcSuvpXhimhiSbV=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "2 years ago",
        "text": "If you're a wine lover and happen to be traveling from Montreal to Ottawa, I highly recommend making a stop at this charming winery. Tucked away in a tranquil location, it offers a serene escape from the hustle and bustle of the city.\nThe owners of the winery are incredibly welcoming and friendly, making you feel right at home as soon as you step through the door. But the real stars of the show are the wines.\nTo complement the wine, the winery also serves up some mouth-watering fresh baked pizza. The aroma alone is enough to get your taste buds tingling, and the taste is even better. It's the perfect pairing to the wine and makes for a truly unforgettable experience.\nOverall, if you're looking for a relaxing and enjoyable winery experience, look no further than this hidden gem. The serene setting, friendly owners, delicious wine, and tasty food make for a truly unforgettable visit.",
        "time": 1684118109,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Albert B",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117669243165505763291/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV489Ao2mlXebUxFsFn97CSoKj4PxviEiAN4q_VBdOk8dUXbp7q=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "6 months ago",
        "text": "Incredible family-owned vineyard! I highly recommend this place for special events and casual hangouts. Vignoble d'Ovils surpassed my expectations. 5 stars, I would love to come again.",
        "time": 1755404977,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Travel Lover",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109022884756264532387/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocLER8NfG5N5RjEbfY_B_ZjZtS9GsSBYMcrdOjNMzt64NTlcUg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "7 months ago",
        "text": "We decided to do a little brewery/winery tour i our area instead of heading to Prince Edward County or Niagara…this was one of our stops.\n\nSaid it was open by the road. Arrived around 5:30 on a Friday. Saw that they had folks to the back setting up for an event. 4 adults parked snd went inside , walked past a bunch of people that didn’t acknowledge us, then went inside, no one came , then after looking st a few products they hay displayed ( 15$/250ml maple syrup!!!) s gentleman came out from a back room  and said hello , are you new here? We said yes . He said well we are setting up for s wedding tomorrow. And we were like:” we see that”\nLong silence so I said so you won’t serve us, we can’t see your products? He said no, sorry.\nSo we left.\nJust awful.\nThe vines are kinda messy and young  ( we also grow about 250 table grape vines ourselves ) and the place doesn’t really seem set up super well. But that was just beyond bad customer service… wow… he could have said let me introduce you to our wines, we are a little busy but if you’d like to go sit over there with a glass you are welcome… or something…we won’t be back.",
        "time": 1751750419,
        "translated": false
      }
    ],
